  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $25,$ and the percentage is $0.6%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.6%=0.6÷100=0.006\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.6%\\times 25 \\\\  & =0.006\\times 25 \\\\  & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.6%$ of $25$ is $0.15.$ \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.6%=\\frac{0.6}{100}=\\frac{0.6\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{6}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.6%\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1,000}\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{150}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.6%$ of $25$ is $0.15.$",
